  "source": "irules",
  "text": "LSN::pool\nDescription\nExplicitly set the LSN pool used for translation.\nSyntax\nLSN\n::\npool\n<\npool_name\n>\nLSN::pool\nSet or override the LSN translation pool used for this connection.\nThe LSN translation pool contains the candidate addresses to which a\nclient address may be translated.\nThis command has no effect if the translation type is deterministic.\nExamples\nRelated Information\nValid Events:\nCLIENT_ACCEPTED\n,\nCLIENT_DATA\n,\nHTTP_REQUEST\n,\nLB_FAILED\n,\nLB_SELECTED\n,\nRTSP_REQUEST\n,\nSIP_REQUEST\nIntroduced: BIGIP-11.3.0\nThe BIG-IP API Reference documentation contains community-contributed content. F5 does not monitor \nor control community code contributions. We make no guarantees or warranties regarding the available code, \nand it may contain errors, defects, bugs, inaccuracies, or security vulnerabilities.  Your access to and use of any \ncode available in the BIG-IP API reference guides is solely at your own risk.",
